Root cause found and fixed in:

- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/timer/timer.c`

### What was wrong
The timer prescaler was configured for a **10× faster timer tick** than intended:

- Broken value: `timer_set_prescaler(... / 5000)`
- Correct value: `timer_set_prescaler(... / 500)`

This directly compresses all Morse element durations (DIT/DAH/spacing) by 10×, so the full sequence appears sped up.

### Fix applied
Updated prescaler line back to:

```c
timer_set_prescaler(TIM2, ((rcc_apb1_frequency * 2) / 500));
```

This restores the intended base timer rate used by the `frequency_sequence[]` values and returns playback tempo to deliberate timing.

### Validation status
- Code diff confirms only this timing-critical line changed.
- Local build attempt was blocked by missing `OPENCM3_DIR` in this environment, so binary rebuild/flash could not be completed here.  
- Logic-level timing analysis confirms this is the direct cause of the accelerated blink pattern.
